From 939e864ad9e82d241aaa2374dc4e23e4ea1856d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:33:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Depth first wave: twelve singing crystals, Old Jaspa's warm
 gems, the pilgrims' waystone

COL-1 (src/game/crystals.js): the collectible layer grows from 6 to 12 crystals, +1 max life each
(10 to 22). The six in the world are unchanged; six more are given by puzzles as owed rewards
(caught up after a load). crystalsAll keeps meaning the six in the world (Sendell's chapter-11
line, old saves); all twelve is dx_crystals12: in the core fight Sendell catches Twinsen once
when his life would reach zero (Hero.damage asks story.depth.catchFall), and an epilogue line.
The slots of DES-1, DES-2, HAM-3 and UND-1 exist with their reward plumbing but are marked
built: false: no quest gives them yet, so 8 of 12 can be had today.

ISL-1 (story/depth.js): Knartas's gem-sorting room gets a low bench with a tray of six stones and
two bins, PROJECT and KEEP. Jaspa's favour follows his own line. Twinsen takes each stone (his
hand on it), says what he sees (two wear a pale crust with dust rising: the dig's rule), and sets
it in a bin. A warm one in PROJECT flashes the bin's lamp and everything goes back on the tray;
right, Jaspa gives a singing crystal. The singing fork makes the warm ones ring.

HAM-1 (story/depth.js): the monastery terrace's waystone gets an upper stone that turns a quarter
at a time, both his hands on its grips, carved dome, roof, ice, houses. Each wrong face says what
it faces; the dome turned to the observatory sinks a slab in the pillar's foot: a crystal in the
niche. Brother Tenpa's hook follows his own line.

State is dx_ flags only, save format 5 unchanged; a save from the build before loads with 16 max
life and 6 of 12. tests/depth-1.mjs plays both puzzles by input, with a wrong attempt and a
Save & quit / Continue in the middle of each, and loads tests/fixtures/pre-col1-save.json (a save
written by db3707df). DEPTH-PLAN.md: the three cards' Built rows.

